    "title": "Data Center Tussle in Paluxy - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mark Henricks ,\n8 hours ago Sometimes the good guys win. A string of victories has raised hopes that citizen groups opposing several large data centers proposed for south of Fort Worth will prevail against the corporations and developers behind the projects. First, NRG pulled its application for an air permit to build a power plant supplying electricity to one huge center near Glen Rose. Then Hood County won a favorable ruling in a lawsuit it was defending against another developer that sued to have its project approved. Read full article",
